WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.980
Good morning Hank, it is Friday December 17th
2010. Time for the Project For Awesome! Is

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.749
that too much? Felt like a lot! Think I actually
hurt my shoulder.

00:00:07.749 --> 00:00:11.540
Today is the day that YouTube is not about
kittens who are inspired by kittens but about

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:14.839
charity. You can participate in the Project
For Awesome all day, and all day tomorrow

00:00:14.839 --> 00:00:21.420
by going to youtube.com/p4a or projectforawesome.com.
All day long, a huge army of commenters, including

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.050
Hank and me, will be running around going
to every Project For Awesome video we can

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:28.890
find and commenting on it like crazy and rating
and favoriting. And this year, there is added

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:31.880
incentive. Nerdfighters, you may know how
much I hate pennies. Well this year, Hank

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:37.980
and I will be donating one penny for every
Project For Awesome comment up to one million

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.980
comments. This year our pennies will go to
benefit 'Save The Children' and 'Partners

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.560
In Health', two charities that Nerdfighteria
has worked with extensively before, which

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.060
I am going to tell you about in a second.
But first I wanna tell you a story.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:50.660
So Hank, a few years ago, just after the invasion
of Iraq, I was watching the news with my friend

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:53.579
Hassan, and they were showing this very nice
house thst had been bombed, and there was

00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:57.399
a huge hole in the wall that had been covered
over with plywood. And on that plywood there

00:00:57.399 --> 00:01:01.210
was all this Arabic graffiti in black spray
paint. And the news guy was talking about

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:04.460
the anger on the Arab street and everything
and then Hassan starts laughing and I say

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:08.329
"What's so funny?" and he said "The graffiti"
and I said "What's funny about it?" He said

00:01:08.329 --> 00:01:12.890
"It says 'Happy Birthday Sir despite the circumstances'".
Hank, the news man and I had fallen into the

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:18.359
same trap. We both assumed it was political,
angry, violent graffiti not "Happy Birthday

00:01:18.359 --> 00:01:22.439
Sir, despite the circumstances" graffiti and
ever since I've been thinking about why we

00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:23.659
fell into that trap.

00:01:23.659 --> 00:01:26.929
As humans we have a bad habit of imagining
people who live far away from us or are in

00:01:26.929 --> 00:01:30.880
different circumstances from us, as fundamentally
'Other'. But in Nerdfighteria we've already

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:34.520
learned that people who live in very different
circumstances from us are not fundamentally

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:37.690
'Other'. We know it because we've seen what
happens when we work with 'Save The Children'

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:41.100
and Shaun's 'Uncultured Project' to build
a Pond Sand Filter in Bangladesh that after

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:45.219
two years is still providing clean water to
all these people. And we know it because with

00:01:45.219 --> 00:01:48.209
the help of the 'Harry Potter Alliance' and
'Partners In Health', we were able to fly

00:01:48.209 --> 00:01:52.219
the SS DFTBA, full of lifesaving supplies
to Haiti. We've already seen what happens

00:01:52.219 --> 00:01:56.319
when you stop seeing people in poverty as
'Other' and start seeing them as part of 'Us'.

00:01:56.319 --> 00:02:00.779
You know 'Us', people who do this to remind
themselves to be awesome. 'Us', people who

00:02:00.779 --> 00:02:04.920
even in the wake of terrible tragedy find
a way to happy dance. We want to keep that

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:08.720
awesome going not only because it helps people
who live in poverty but also because it helps

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:13.390
us. It reminds us that when we look at graffiti
that we don't understand, it very may well

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:16.680
say "Happy Birthday Sir, despite the circumstances".

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:21.099
So every Project For Awesome comment, up to
a million comments is worth one penny to 'Partners

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:24.019
in Health' or 'Save The Children'. And if
you go to projectforawesome.com right now,

00:02:24.019 --> 00:02:28.239
you'll find lots of amazing ways to donate
to great organizations. We've got raffle prizes

00:02:28.239 --> 00:02:32.629
from Meekakitty and WheezyWaiter and Nerimon
and Ryan Higa and tons of other YouTubers

00:02:32.629 --> 00:02:36.409
and lots of awesome nerdfighter raffles including
the chance to win my nerd glasses and the

00:02:36.409 --> 00:02:41.049
last remaining BobbleJohn. Also, everyone
who enters my zombie apocalypse novella raffle

00:02:41.049 --> 00:02:45.549
will be emailed the story, and one lucky winner
will receive the actual printed version of

00:02:45.549 --> 00:02:49.870
the story, extensively annotated by me and
signed for the winner. But in my opinion,

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:54.931
the best raffle is the one where if you win,
your name will be the name of Hank's new album.

00:02:54.931 --> 00:02:59.659
Like if the winner of the raffle's name is
Jeff, Hank's new album will be called 'Jeff'.

00:02:59.659 --> 00:03:01.969
I'm gonna enter that one like 400 times.

00:03:01.969 --> 00:03:06.709
So please go over to projectforawesome.com
to donate and join us all day today and tomorrow

00:03:06.709 --> 00:03:13.170
